# Coding standards (split by topic)

Large standards were split so Cursor can apply **shorter, scoped** rules. Use the table below; legacy links to “coding-standards” mean **this index + the relevant split file**.

| Topic | Rule file |
|-------|-----------|
| URLs, env, auth, proxy, `fetch` clients, query params, tenancy, validation, logging, dev workflow | `api-and-auth.mdc` |
| Prisma modules, migrations, drift, pooling | `database-prisma.mdc` |
| `storageService`, GCS, AI vision/attachments | `storage-and-ai-attachments.mdc` |
| `shared/components`, contrast | `ui-standards.mdc` |
| TypeScript / `any` policy, routers, Prisma JSON | `typescript-quality.mdc` |

**Modules (landing, AI context, trash, manifests, notifications):** `module-development.mdc` + **`docs/guides/MODULE_DEVELOPMENT_LONG_REFERENCE.md`**.

**Also use:** `backend-trust-boundaries.mdc`, `frontend-proxy-auth-consistency.mdc`, `module-interoperability.mdc`, `release-safety-gates.mdc`.

**Last updated:** 2026-05-05
